                    briefing_text_r4:       `The Brazilian entry is imminent. Sequence the funded projects against the <strong>5-month</strong> and <strong>9-month</strong> clocks — a <em>balanced</em> plan defends home on the 5-month clock and certifies for the 9-month EU window, rather than chasing technical elegance at 14 months. Run a cash-runway check: the spend is front-loaded and revenue lags two quarters, so hold a sensible reserve. Define the contingency — <strong>cut EU first</strong> to protect the home cash engine — and pitch a plan to the board that can still make payroll.`,

